<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios-Nov 28.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios-Nov 28.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Highest and lowest price earnings ratios for Australian companies included in the 320-company All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on Wednesday. P/E based on rolling 12 months earnings.</p>
<p>Highest 10</p>
<p>Rank Name		     P/E    Close</p>
<p> 1 Tourism Asset	  3666.67   1.10</p>
<p> 2 Portman Min	     387.30   2.44</p>
<p> 3 Niugini Min	     233.81   3.25</p>
<p> 4 Mayne Nickless	  175.50   7.95</p>
<p> 5 TNT			 172.66   2.40</p>
<p> 6 Colonial Coml	   120.22   2.20</p>
<p> 7 Adel Bton Cement	118.12   1.63</p>
<p> 8 Forrestania Gold	 93.19   2.60</p>
<p> 9 Herald Rsc		 85.84   0.97</p>
<p>10 Westral Forest	   83.33   2.30</p>
<p>Lowest 10</p>
<p> 1 Dominion Min		1.86   0.81</p>
<p> 2 Computer Power	    3.96   4.05</p>
<p> 3 Premier Inv		 4.17   0.74</p>
<p> 4 BTR Plc		     5.59   5.20</p>
<p> 5 Queensland Cotton	 5.67   4.30</p>
<p> 6 Parbury Ltd		 6.08   0.72</p>
<p> 7 Aust Gold Rsc	     7.23   1.32</p>
<p> 8 OLS Asia Hldgs	    7.56   0.90</p>
<p> 9 RGC			   7.69   5.30</p>
<p>10 Templeton Global	  8.00   1.40</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
